        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(scripts): bound release CI summary GitHub lookups",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe release CI summary helper performs multiple sequential `gh` API reads during full release validation. Each read used `execFileSync` without a timeout, so one stalled GitHub request could block the surrounding workflow job until the 120-minute budget expires.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe default `gh` runner now routes through a caller-owned `execFileSync` with a 60-second timeout and `SIGKILL`, and applies the same bound to artifact zip downloads. This keeps the release-specific latency budget local, preserves the existing 64 MiB output allowance, covers all lookups (REST reads and artifact zip downloads), and continues to fail closed when a lookup cannot complete.\n\nThe runner accepts an `execFileSyncImpl` injection point and an optional `timeoutMs` parameter, allowing the exact production options and error propagation to be tested without a slow timer-based test.\n\n## User Impact\n\nA release CI summary lookup no longer waits indefinitely on a stalled GitHub request. Healthy validation behavior is unchanged; a lookup that exceeds one minute now fails clearly so the release can be diagnosed or retried.\n\n## Evidence\n\nExact head: \\`${HEAD_SHA}\\`, based on `593423ecc0d3c1d883e247a6fca568e312791eec`.\n\n- Focused test: `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run test/scripts/release-ci-summary.test.ts` - 45/45 passed (including 4 `runReleaseCiGh` tests).\n- **Real behavior proof — timeout kill**: A 1 ms timeout against a real `gh api rate_limit` subprocess correctly triggers SIGKILL and throws, proving the timeout+killSignal surface works on actual child processes (not only injected mocks).\n- **Real behavior proof — healthy completion**: A fast `node -e 0` subprocess with the production 60-second bound completes successfully, proving the timeout does not false-positive on healthy completions.\n- Targeted `oxlint` and `git diff --check origin/main...HEAD` passed.",
